<BaseLayout lang="en" title="Résumé" description="Résumé of Mateus Reis Bastos, an IT Infrastructure Intern and Communication Network Engineering student at UnB.">
  <div class="resume-page shell">
    <header class="page-heading">
      <h1>Mateus Reis Bastos</h1>
      <p>IT Infrastructure Intern · Blue Team, SOC and cybersecurity · Network Engineering — UnB</p>
      <div class="resume-contact" aria-label="Location and career objective">
        <span>Brasília, Federal District, Brazil</span>
        <span>Seeking an information-security internship — on-site, hybrid, or remote</span>
      </div>
    </header>

    <section class="resume-section">
      <h2>Profile</h2>
      <div>
        <p class="resume-intro">Communication Network Engineering student at the University of Brasília, focused on information security and infrastructure. I am building hands-on experience in monitoring, access control, and observability, combining a defensive SOC perspective with CTF practice and offensive-security studies.</p>
        <p>I currently work at Associação GigaCandanga and am part of the management team at UnBreakable, UnB's offensive-security study group. I am seeking an information-security internship in Brasília or remotely.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="resume-section">
      <h2>Experience</h2>
      <div>
        <article class="resume-entry">
          <header>
            <h3>IT Infrastructure Intern</h3>
            <p>Associação GigaCandanga · Nov 2025 – present · Brasília, Brazil · hybrid</p>
          </header>
          <p>Associação GigaCandanga is a Science and Technology Institution responsible for managing Redecomep, the metropolitan education and research network of Brazil's Federal District. The network connects UnB, research institutes, and government agencies through high-speed optical infrastructure.</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Contribute to the research and early engineering stage of a SOC project through feasibility studies, technical documentation reviews, and security-tool mapping for the defensive architecture.</li>
            <li>Run laboratory proofs of concept with Wazuh and Suricata for Linux server security monitoring and event analysis, with production implementation planned for the project's next stages.</li>
            <li>Studied and validated JumpServer in a test environment as a PAM solution, configuring a Bastion Host for centralized access, session auditing, and secure SSH policies.</li>
            <li>Assist with Linux system administration and the operation of Zabbix and Grafana for high-capacity network observability.</li>
          </ul>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="resume-section">
      <h2>Academic &amp; community work</h2>
      <div>
        <article class="resume-entry">
          <header>
            <h3>Management team member and Recon instructor — UnBreakable</h3>
            <p>UnB offensive-security study group · Mar 2026 – present</p>
          </header>
          <p>I am part of UnBreakable's management team and one of the instructors for Recon, its entry-level cohort. The group is organized by UnB students for competitions, research, and technical practice on platforms such as TryHackMe and Hack The Box.</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Helped structure and run the 2026 selection process: two weeks of hands-on classes, elimination challenges, and a mandatory write-up as the final stage; 29 participants were admitted.</li>
            <li>Led seven weekly Recon activities with TryHackMe machines, each accompanied by a technical write-up.</li>
          </ul>
        </article>

        <article class="resume-entry">
          <header>
            <h3>Member — IEEE ComSoc UnB</h3>
            <p>IEEE Communications Society student chapter · May 2025 – Mar 2026</p>
          </header>
          <p>Participated in communication-networking projects and events. Volunteered at the IEEE ComSoc Student Leadership Tech Conference for Brazil's Central-Northern region in October 2025, supporting the event's organization and delivery.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="resume-section">
      <h2>Education</h2>
      <div class="resume-entry">
        <header>
          <h3>Bachelor's Degree in Communication Network Engineering</h3>
          <p>University of Brasília (UnB) · in progress</p>
        </header>
        <p>Multidisciplinary training in Electrical Engineering, Networks, and Computing.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="resume-section">
